.DS_Store

# The two production dumps at the root contain registrant PII. The blanket
# *.sql rule that keeps them out was also silently swallowing new database
# migrations — the two 2026-08-19 failed_notifications files are only tracked
# because they were committed in the old public_html repo before this rule
# existed. Migrations are code and must ship with a deploy, so exempt them.
*.sql
!public_html/database/migrations/*.sql
!cpd.prosper-minds.com/database/migrations/*.sql
# Same problem for the local-dev seed overrides: docker-compose.yml mounts them
# by name, and local-dev/verify.sh now depends on the local admin account one of
# them creates, so a fresh clone could not bring the stack up without them.
# They contain placeholder values only — no production credentials, no PII.
!local-dev/*.sql

/*.md
!/README.md
local-dev/logs/
/*.pdf
